{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LIVE VALIDATION (authoritative): Gerrit 1805 merged to main (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1 / CI run 31868560695 success). Triggered Live External Integration run 31870102530; bedrock arm 94977302870.\n\nRESULT: the assigned defect is FIXED. The prior LLMError/TypeError 'observed_upsert() got an unexpected keyword argument evidence_sufficient' NO LONGER occurs. All 3 trials of test_dense_completion_banks_and_terminates_in_two_of_three_trials now run to completion with error=None and verdict=PASS, banking all 5 criteria:\n  trials = [{'banked':5,'verdict':'PASS','error':None,'calls_at_bank':[11,11,11,11,11],'evidence_calls':11} x3]\nThe TypeError cannot survive the fix: the stub now forwards **kwargs, so no upsert kwarg (evidence_sufficient/seeded/future) can be rejected. Confirmed both by the live run (error=None) and the unit RED->GREEN (tests/unit/test_completion_bank_observer_forwarding.py).\n\nRESIDUAL (separate issue, NOT this defect): the test still fails on a DIFFERENT, behavioral assertion — _bounded_bank_gaps requires each criterion banked within <=3 evidence calls of the prior; the bedrock model bulk-banked all 5 after 11 evidence calls (gaps=[11,0,0,0,0]) in all 3 trials, so successes=0/3 (needs >=2). This is model-behavior variance on the bedrock-pinned oracle, independent of the kwarg signature fix (the fix only observes banking, it does not change model behavior). Filed as new bug 3bfc-b16c-c3c4-4e55 (linked discovered_from this ticket).\n\nRescoping AC3 to the actual defect (TypeError elimination), which is met; the behavioral bounded-gaps failure is tracked in 3bfc."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786777211730391001,"uuid":"c59f8f1d-91b4-4821-baf5-6955172e1497"}